WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:02.780
Okay, let's get into audience questions for
the week.

00:00:02.780 --> 00:00:05.760
I genuinely love this first question I have,
I'll have to say about it.

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:06.760
Hey David.

00:00:06.760 --> 00:00:07.760
What, what

00:00:07.760 --> 00:00:09.590
wastes of money are you shocked people still
fall for?

00:00:09.590 --> 00:00:14.139
Um, I, there's like a big one which I'm going
to lead up to, but a couple of small things

00:00:14.139 --> 00:00:19.109
are, I am always surprised when people buy
insurance on relatively small purchases.

00:00:19.109 --> 00:00:25.310
And I understand the, um, idea that if it's
something very expensive, uh, you actually

00:00:25.310 --> 00:00:31.119
may suffer a hardship if it breaks and you
have to fix it or replace it.

00:00:31.119 --> 00:00:36.730
I can understand getting an insurance policy
replacement plan, extended warranty or whatever,

00:00:36.730 --> 00:00:40.430
but particularly as someone who worked at
circuit city and sold a lot of these, uh,

00:00:40.430 --> 00:00:45.699
inexpensive and service plans and stuff like
that, it really doesn't make sense on small

00:00:45.699 --> 00:00:46.780
purchases.

00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:49.219
And I don't know why anybody you continues
to buy it.

00:00:49.219 --> 00:00:54.450
And the way I, I now don't get insurance on
anything, no service plans, no warranties,

00:00:54.450 --> 00:00:55.450
any of that stuff.

00:00:55.450 --> 00:01:00.430
And the calculation I've made is that all
of the stuff I never got insurance on and

00:01:00.430 --> 00:01:01.989
it never broke.

00:01:01.989 --> 00:01:07.189
That's thousands upon thousands of dollars
in insurance dollars that I never spent.

00:01:07.189 --> 00:01:12.670
So I'm so far ahead at this point that I feel
like I'm properly kind of like self insured

00:01:12.670 --> 00:01:13.670
health insurance.

00:01:13.670 --> 00:01:19.260
Of course I have, um, you know, home insurance,
I think I have to have it, but I have that.

00:01:19.260 --> 00:01:25.740
But, um, insurance plans on really inexpensive
items I think are a waste of money in general.

00:01:25.740 --> 00:01:28.119
Stuff that people don't use and don't cancel.

00:01:28.119 --> 00:01:32.540
I'm still surprised at the number of people
of friends I have who say I really got to

00:01:32.540 --> 00:01:37.290
cancel that, a credit monitoring thing or
whatever.

00:01:37.290 --> 00:01:38.290
I never look at it.

00:01:38.290 --> 00:01:42.280
I don't even know what my access code is,
but I just keep paying the 25 bucks a month.

00:01:42.280 --> 00:01:43.509
You got to cancel that stuff.

00:01:43.509 --> 00:01:45.439
That is a stunning waste of money to me.

00:01:45.439 --> 00:01:51.980
But the really, the big one that shocks me,
how are people still falling for pyramid schemes?

00:01:51.980 --> 00:01:58.500
And as it has been more friendly, uh, uh,
more sort of appealingly renamed multilevel

00:01:58.500 --> 00:01:59.910
marketing.

00:01:59.910 --> 00:02:02.070
I don't know how people still fall for it.

00:02:02.070 --> 00:02:06.450
The number of people I'm friends with on Facebook
that are doing a whole bunch of these multilevel

00:02:06.450 --> 00:02:10.500
marketing things, uh, is, is absolutely shocking
to me.

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:15.830
And whenever it comes up in sort of social
settings, I, I, I'm not trying to have huge

00:02:15.830 --> 00:02:18.390
conflicts with people in my personal life.

00:02:18.390 --> 00:02:25.270
So I will often be very, very polite and actually
say, Oh, uh, eh, how many sales have you actually

00:02:25.270 --> 00:02:26.270
made?

00:02:26.270 --> 00:02:30.640
And they'll say, well, you know, for now I
really only purchased my supply of stuff.

00:02:30.640 --> 00:02:34.720
Um, so that I have demos and I've only made
like a sailor too.

00:02:34.720 --> 00:02:36.910
And I say, Oh, okay.

00:02:36.910 --> 00:02:40.720
Um, so, but now you have all that stuff that
you can sell over the next few months.

00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:44.620
And they'll say, well, actually, you're in
order to remain as a reseller, you actually

00:02:44.620 --> 00:02:46.290
have to place an order every month.

00:02:46.290 --> 00:02:51.240
And then I say, oh, so every month you actually
have more stuff you have to buy regardless

00:02:51.240 --> 00:02:53.210
of whether you're making any sales.

00:02:53.210 --> 00:02:57.170
And they say, yeah, you do, but I'm building
my business and all this stuff.

00:02:57.170 --> 00:03:01.980
It's stunning, stunning to me that people
are still falling for that stuff.

00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:07.700
And I think I get one aspect of it, which
is wages have been stagnant for however long

00:03:07.700 --> 00:03:08.990
they've been stagnant.

00:03:08.990 --> 00:03:12.710
Um, people are looking to make some extra
money.

00:03:12.710 --> 00:03:13.880
People want autonomy.

00:03:13.880 --> 00:03:20.090
So all of these MLMs and pyramid schemes are
designed to prey upon people who say, Hey,

00:03:20.090 --> 00:03:25.080
okay, I have a job and I don't want to leave
that job, but I would like a little extra

00:03:25.080 --> 00:03:26.080
money.

00:03:26.080 --> 00:03:31.670
I would like to build my own business and
be my own boss and work on my own time.

00:03:31.670 --> 00:03:34.640
And uh, that's why people fall for it because
it is appealing.

00:03:34.640 --> 00:03:36.260
It is actually appealing.

00:03:36.260 --> 00:03:39.240
Um, but it is so, so pernicious.

00:03:39.240 --> 00:03:45.360
And of course the number of people who even
make back their initial investment is relatively

00:03:45.360 --> 00:03:46.360
small.

00:03:46.360 --> 00:03:47.360
Nevermind.

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:51.140
You know, the number of people, whoever make
over $1,000 period with any of these things

00:03:51.140 --> 00:03:56.510
in profit is so astronomically small and you're
always told about the success stories don't

00:03:56.510 --> 00:03:57.510
fall for it.

00:03:57.510 --> 00:03:58.510
Don't fall for it.

00:03:58.510 --> 00:04:04.271
There is a, there are endless resources online
about all of the companies that are Mlms and

00:04:04.271 --> 00:04:05.271
pyramid schemes.

00:04:05.271 --> 00:04:09.530
You'll notice, I haven't named any of them
in this segment because a lot of those companies

00:04:09.530 --> 00:04:13.440
are very, very litigious and I'm not interested
in that.

00:04:13.440 --> 00:04:14.460
But please stop.

00:04:14.460 --> 00:04:15.570
And this is also to my friends.

00:04:15.570 --> 00:04:16.780
Please, please stop.

00:04:16.780 --> 00:04:22.220
You're falling for scams and um, it just get
focused on improving yourself.

00:04:22.220 --> 00:04:26.040
Start a real small business if that's what
you're interested in doing.

00:04:26.040 --> 00:04:30.460
Look at just working a little more or developing
your skills so that you can get a promotion.

00:04:30.460 --> 00:04:35.500
I think that those are much better uses of
time and money than participating in these

00:04:35.500 --> 00:04:36.380
MLM nonsense schemes.

